\section{Analysis}
Ablations show that prefix reuse accounts for most of the latency
saving, and that the eviction policy trades little accuracy for its
memory bound. Per-dataset variance across seeds is below 0.4 F1.

\section{Conclusion}
CAG-Lite improves long-context question answering over open baselines
while halving prefill cost. A controlled comparison with proprietary
systems remains future work.
